# - Shazam, Payé (feat. Youry Ymw) by Wizito (search results, 2026-10-20; the Shazam page itself misloaded on open, so facts are taken from the indexed Shazam listing): released February 8, 2023, by YMW Tolly Boys, as Payé (feat. Youry Ymw) - Single; genre listed as World; 170 BPM; composition and lyrics credit Bernard Robert Gumbs, songwriter.
# - Shazam, Love Me by Wizito (search results, 2026-10-20): released February 14, 2024, by YMW TOLLY BOYS, as Love Me - Single; genre listed as World; 157 BPM; composition and lyrics credit Bernard Gumbs, songwriter; production and engineering credit Sylvio Benjamin, producer.
# - Shazam, TunTun (feat. Ti Al & Dj Chimik) by Wizito (search results, 2026-10-20): released August 1, 2025, label YMW TOLLY BOYS; 164 BPM; performing artists Ti Al, harmony vocals, and Bernard Gumbs, harmony vocals; composition and lyrics Ti Al and Bernard Gumbs, songwriters; production and engineering Dj Chimik, producer.
# - Get Familiar podcast, via Ivy.fm tag page (opened 2026-10-20): mix presented as featuring some of the local releases for St Maarten Carnival 2024; tracklist includes Wizito YMW - Love Me (Dirty), alongside King Kembe, Tolly Boys circle names and other St Maarten carnival releases. This is the only published source consulted that places a Wizito release in a named place circuit, Saint Martin / St Maarten carnival, and the profile attributes the placement to that mix.
# - Shazam, Tolly Boy’s YMW listings (search results, 2026-10-20): Get on Bad (feat. Ciio & King Kembe), released December 30, 2018, and GoDownGoDown, both with songwriter credits to Youry Fleming / Fleming Youry. Cited only to document the YMW Tolly Boys circle around Youry, the featured artist on Payé. No Tolly Boys record is credited to Wizito in this profile.
# Note: this is a THIN record. Only three Wizito releases are verified in the sources above. No verified hometown, birth date, biography interview or official social URL for Bernard Gumbs was confirmed, so none is printed and sameAs is empty. The full name is printed in two forms exactly as the credits publish them: Bernard Gumbs on Love Me and TunTun, Bernard Robert Gumbs on Payé. YMW Tolly Boys, the label and circle on the Wizito releases, is not the Saint Lucia artist Tallyboy who has a page on this site, and Sylvio Benjamin, producer of Love Me, is not presented as any relation of Wayne Benjamin (Benji): the shared surname is a coincidence of credits, with no published link.

